Client-core jars go here.

The launcher looks in this directory for the jar named by a template in
launcher/src/main/profiles.ts — <repo>/artifacts in development, and
<resourcesPath>/artifacts in a packaged build.

Nothing needs to be here.

Two different "no core" cases, and they are reported differently on purpose:

  - No core exists for that version and loader at all. The instance card says
    so up front, before anything is downloaded.
  - A core is named for that version and loader, but the jar is not on disk.
    Only discoverable at launch, so it is reported then: the instance starts
    without it and the runtime log names the path it looked for.

Neither is a broken install. The instance is a complete, working Minecraft
setup either way.
